        "greeting": "Dear friend,",
        "letter": "<p>I started Pups Around the World because I've spent twenty-five years painting people's favorite places, and somewhere along the way I noticed the thing missing from most portraits wasn't the person. It was their dog.</p><p>I curate every scene in this collection myself, the palette, the light, the mood, long before your pup ever steps into it. Paris isn't Paris because a prompt said so. It's Paris because I know what that light actually looks like in the evening, and I wanted your dog standing in it.</p><p>I still believe the artist should lead and the tools should follow, not the other way around. That's the whole idea behind every portrait here: your dog, painted the way I'd paint anyone I loved, somewhere I'd want to send them.</p>",
